<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Sosso kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1180 CE – 1235 CE (approx.) · capital Sosso</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Soninke kingdom whose blacksmith-king Sumanguru Kante seized the Ghana Empire's heartland before being defeated by Sundiata Keita.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sosso-empire">Sosso</a> grew out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaniaga">Kaniaga</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soninke">Soninke</a> province of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ghana-empire">Ghana Empire</a> north of the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a>. As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a> weakened in the 12th century, the Kante clan, associated with blacksmithing and its power objects, made Sosso independent and began conquering neighbouring lands.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumanguru-kante">Sumanguru Kante</a>, who ruled in the early 13th century, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sosso-empire">Sosso</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koumbi-saleh">Koumbi Saleh</a>, the old capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>, and subdued the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mande-peoples">Mande</a> chiefdoms, including the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kangaba">Kingdom of Kangaba</a>. Oral tradition portrays him as a powerful sorcerer and a harsh ruler, and links him with resistance to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, though such details come from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sundiata-keita">Sundiata</a> epic.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mande-peoples">Mande</a> clans rallied behind <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sundiata-keita">Sundiata Keita</a>, who defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumanguru-kante">Sumanguru</a> at the battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kirina">Kirina</a> around 1235. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sosso-empire">Sosso</a> was absorbed into the new <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mali-empire">Mali Empire</a>, and the epic of its fall is still performed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/griots">griots</a> across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1180 CE – 1235 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">West Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:83.18%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1180 CE – 1235 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sosso</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sumanguru Kante</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Soninke traditional religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Soninke</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mali">Mali</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Sosso, Soso, Kaniaga</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1208&amp;focus=sosso-kingdom" aria-label="Sosso kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4614 1483 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sosso kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4782 1851h0M4769 1989h0M4769 1989h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4934 1739h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4934 1739h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Mali. <a href="/atlas?year=1208&amp;focus=sosso-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
